.TH HASHMAP_PUT 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
hashmap_put \- Add or update a key-value pair in a hashmap

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/hashmap.h>

.IB void
.IB hashmap_put(hashmap* map, const char* key, void* val);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBhashmap_put\fR function adds or updates a key-value pair in a hashmap. It takes a pointer to the hashmap, a key, and a value as arguments.

The function takes the following parameters:
.IB hashmap*
A pointer to the hashmap where the key-value pair will be added or updated.
.IB const char*
The key to be added or updated.
.IB void*
The value to be associated with the key.

The function adds or updates the key-value pair in the hashmap. If the key already exists, its value is updated.

The \fBhashmap_put\fR function is intended to be used to add or update key-value pairs in a hashmap.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBhashmap_put\fR function to add or update a key-value pair in a hashmap:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/hashmap.h>

int main() {
    hashmap map;

    hashmap_init(&map);

    hashmap_put(&map, "example", "value");

    // map now contains the key-value pair "example" -> "value"

    return 0;
}
.nef